<chapter xml:id="ch11-chapter-theory-1m1p" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Classical Inference Methods</title>

  <introduction>
    <p> [This may become an appendix.] This chapter introduces the idea of the normal distribution (and later the t-distribution) and how it can
       be used to theoretically model sampling distributions for the purpose of performing inference. This chapter focuses on inference, 
       hypothesis testing and confidence intervals, for one mean and one proportion.
        </p>
  </introduction>



